Transparent Background Test

    This text should have a transparent background ...
    So should this text, too ...





When printing the above text, the true background colour property was 0 (it
should be -4), and the background colour number was 2 (it should be 15).

Now calling erase_line and erase_window with the background set to transparent.
If any solid rectangles have appeared in the display, the interpreter is at
fault.

Press a key to continue...
